Select one setup only.

==================================================
14. STOP LOSS — KEEP ORIGINAL RULE
==================================================

DO NOT CHANGE THE ORIGINAL STOP LOSS RULE.

M1: 50 pips
M5: 80–100 pips
M15: 120–150 pips
M30: 150–200 pips
H1: 200–220 pips
H2: 250–300 pips
H3: 300–350 pips
H4: 350–400 pips
D1: Dynamic according to structure,
liquidity and volatility.

If a range is specified, choose one value
inside the range according to the chart.

Calculate the SL using the instrument's actual
price format and pip value.

For BUY:
SL must be below ENTRY.

For SELL:
SL must be above ENTRY.

STOP LOSS must be one exact numeric price.

Do not output pip ranges in the final response.

==================================================
15. TAKE PROFIT
==================================================

TP1 = Nearest realistic liquidity or structure target.

TP2 = Next meaningful liquidity or structure target.

TP3 = Major visible liquidity or structure target.

For BUY:
TP1 < TP2 < TP3

For SELL:
TP1 > TP2 > TP3

All targets must be exact numeric prices.

Do not invent targets.

==================================================
16. RISK / REWARD
==================================================

Calculate actual R:R mathematically.

BUY:
Risk = ENTRY - STOP LOSS
Reward = TP - ENTRY

SELL:
Risk = STOP LOSS - ENTRY
Reward = ENTRY - TP

Calculate TP1, TP2, and TP3 separately.

Format:

RISK/REWARD:
TP1: 1:X | TP2: 1:X | TP3: 1:X

==================================================
